  "description": "Some days speed and efficiency are king, and we need to get to the finish line - fast. Other days, gravel roads beckon us to explore off the beaten path. With its split personality - both race-oriented and self-sufficient - the Buzzard is ready for it all. Our versatile carbon gravel bike has a long front triangle for stability and a short rear end with flared chain stays that make it easy to whip through tight singletrack. In-frame downtube storage and 18 mounts accommodate racks, fenders and panniers for multi-day adventure rides. Internal cable routing, UDH compatibility and space for wide tires (up to a 45c in the rear) make the Buzzard sleek and functional. Whether it's a quick gravel grind, a destination race, or an epic bikepacking adventure, the Buzzard will take you on roads less traveled.\n\nBuilt on a lightweight carbon frame and fork, the Top Shelf Buzzard is spec'd for the most efficient combination of speed and technical performance. Featuring a SRAM Force 1x group, FSA SL-K AGX tubeless carbon wheels and Vittoria Terreno Dry gravel tires, it's our race-day rig. Plus, a RockShox Reverb wireless dropper post lets you drop your saddle for those spicy drop-bar descents.",
